# The shelf is set up in a step of its own: `open_shelf` builds it on the folder it decides, `out`, and gives it back;
# `main` then keeps the report and the log on it. Each method names its own file in the folder and hands the path to
# `write`, so the file is whole where both are: the step that set the shelf up, which ran before, and the method on the
# calls that lead to `write` (#309). Under `keep_report` the route writes the report alone, under `keep_log` the log
# alone. The shelf goes from the step that built it to `main`, and each method hands it on to `write` (`self.root` is
# a projection of it).

route shelf.cli.main
step main/open_shelf
step main/open_shelf/Shelf()
step main/Shelf.keep_report
step main/Shelf.keep_report/write
step main/Shelf.keep_log
step main/Shelf.keep_log/write

line entry > main call
line main/open_shelf/Shelf() > Shelf@main/open_shelf/Shelf() value
line Shelf@main/open_shelf/Shelf() > main/open_shelf value               # the shelf built goes back
line main/open_shelf > Shelf·shelf@main/open_shelf value
line Shelf·shelf@main/open_shelf > main/Shelf.keep_report/write value     # `write(self.root / "report.txt", text)`
line Shelf·shelf@main/open_shelf > main/Shelf.keep_log/write value        # `write(self.root / "log.txt", text)`
line main/Shelf.keep_report/write > File(out/report.txt) own
line main/Shelf.keep_log/write > File(out/log.txt) own

home Shelf@main/open_shelf/Shelf() main/open_shelf
home Shelf·shelf@main/open_shelf main

side entry left
side File(out/report.txt) right
side File(out/log.txt) right
